{"claim": "The workbench's delete-command Revert re-authors from the journal entry: delete_command's `old` is {command, impl} record data with attachments INLINED (store.get_data reads attachment keys back), so upsert_command(lang, returntype, params, import, body from impl[ext]) — write_flow_body for flows — restores the command; desc/tags/groups are then re-applied from the same `old` because upsert_command carries neither and does not journal, so the restore leaves no second journal entry.", "detail": "Shipped in commit 202584d7 (branch workbench-commands-redesign). The body key is rs for rust, the lang name otherwise (python/flow). The delete toast is the workbench's OWN persistent .wb-toast with a Revert action — the frame toast auto-hides at 2.6s and has no action slot, and the spec forbade touching dev.toast.", "tags": "dev.workbench,delete_command,revert,journal,toast", "confidence": "high", "time": 1793224953699},
